UPDATE companies SET description='Foodberry is based in Boston, Massachusetts. The company was founded by David Edwards, a longtime Harvard professor and founder of AIR and Sensory Cloud, with its proprietary food‑tech platform initially developed in labs at Harvard and MIT before moving into a first‑of‑its‑kind manufacturing facility.

Foodberry creates bite‑sized snacks using a plant‑based coating technology that turns virtually any food or beverage into a self‑contained, no‑mess product. The company operates a 42,000‑square‑foot, GFSI/SQF Level 2‑certified production facility in Boston and offers three core services: product development with an in‑house R&D team, co‑manufacturing for brand partners, and technology transfer to integrate its coating process into existing production lines.

Its customers are food and beverage brands seeking growth‑driving snack innovations. Publicly named partners include the Bel Group (parent of Laughing Cow and GoGo SqueeZ), Van Leeuwen Ice Cream, Gopuff, and Cape Cod Select, with collaborations spanning fruit‑based snacks, ice‑cream bonbons, and frozen smoothie bites.

The venture was started to tackle two systemic problems: making convenient, craveable foods without sacrificing nutrition, and reducing plastic packaging across the food system. Foodberry’s stated aim is to make the future of snacking as nutritious, delicious, and planet‑friendly as a natural berry.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF','GFSI / SQF Level 2']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Development", "Co-Manufacturing", "Tech Transfer"], "industries": ["Food & beverage", "Snack foods", "Fruit snacks"], "materials": ["Plant-based coatings", "Fruit", "Ice cream", "Yogurt", "Smoothie"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary plant\u2011based coating platform that transforms any food or beverage into bite\u2011sized snacks", "42,000 sq ft GFSI/SQF Level 2 certified co\u2011manufacturing facility in Boston", "End\u2011to\u2011end services: product development, co\u2011manufacturing, and technology transfer", "Established partnerships with major brands including Bel Group, Van Leeuwen, and Gopuff", "Mission\u2011driven focus on nutrition and packaging reduction"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Boston, Massachusetts -> db", "Founder David Edwards, Harvard professor -> /about-us", "Technology developed at Harvard and MIT -> /about-us", "42,000 sq ft production facility in Boston, MA -> /", "GFSI / SQF Level 2 certified -> /", "Services: Product Development, Co-Manufacturing, Tech Transfer -> /", "Partners: Bel Group, Van Leeuwen, Gopuff, Cape Cod Select -> /", "Mission: resolve challenges of convenient nutritious foods and plastic packaging -> /about-us", "Certification: SQF -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Foodberry is an innovation company that partners with leading brands to create better bite-sized snacks and operates a 42,000 sq ft production facility in Boston for co-manufacturing.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code":