UPDATE companies SET description='Forj Medical is headquartered in Arden Hills, Minnesota, with additional facilities in St. Paul and Vadnais Heights. The company operates as a global contract design and manufacturing organization (CDMO) focused exclusively on medical devices.

The CDMO provides end-to-end services from design and development through high-volume production. Its vertically integrated capabilities include precision molding, PCBA manufacturing, automation, cable assembly, cleanroom operations, polymer and metal 3D printing, and supply chain management. Forj Medical reports assembling more than 250 million devices and components annually across 450,000 square feet of manufacturing space spread over six global sites in the United States, Costa Rica, Singapore, and Indonesia. The company supports programs ranging from 10 units to 10 million units per project.

Forj Medical serves medical device OEMs across application areas such as fluid and gas management, surgical energy, optical systems, electromagnetic navigation systems and sensors, stimulation and active wearables, and consumables and components. Named customers include Conavi Medical, a Fortune 500 medical device manufacturer, and Vocxi Health, which partnered with Forj to miniaturize a breath-based cancer detection platform.

The company positions itself as a single-source partner that becomes an extension of its clients'' teams, offering integrated quality management (ISO 13485 certified with five FDA establishment registrations) and a digital portal for continuous project visibility. Clients cite Forj''s willingness to redesign systems from the ground up and maintain collaboration under one roof as they scale toward regulatory clearance.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','CE Mark','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision Molding", "PCBA Manufacturing", "Automation", "Cable Assembly", "Cleanrooms", "Polymer & Metal 3D Printing", "Supply Chain Management", "Service & Maintenance", "Sustaining Engineering", "Packaging & Shipping", "Design for Manufacturing", "Design for Automation & Scale", "Custom Prototyping", "Process & Test Development", "Quality & Regulatory Excellence", "Design for Excellence (DFX)", "Full Medical Device System Development", "Custom Electromechanical System Design", "Electromagnetic Sensors & Assemblies", "Microelectronics", "Microcatheters & Access Sheaths", "Capital Systems", "Fluid & Gas Management", "Surgical Energy"], "industries": ["Fluid & Gas Management", "Surgical Energy", "Optical Systems", "Electromagnetic Navigation Systems & Sensors", "Stimulation & Active Wearables", "Consumables & Components"], "materials": ["Polymers", "Metals"], "equipment": [], "volume": "10 units to 10 million per project; 250+ million devices and components assembled annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source CDMO scaling from 10 units to 10 million per project", "Vertically integrated in-house capabilities: molding, PCBA, automation, cable assembly, cleanrooms, 3D printing", "ISO 13485 certified with five FDA establishment registrations", "Global footprint: 450,000 ft\u00b2 across six facilities in the US, Costa Rica, Singapore, Indonesia", "Vital Link Portal providing 24/7 access to project management and compliance documentation"], "facts_used": ["250+ million devices and components assembled per year -> /", "4+ million combined hours of medical device engineering -> /", "450K ft\u00b2 manufacturing space across 6 global facilities -> /", "Headquarters in Arden Hills, MN -> /", "Facilities in St. Paul, MN; Vadnais Heights, MN; Costa Rica; Singapore; Indonesia -> /", "ISO 13485 certified with five FDA Establishment Registrations -> /", "Processes: Precision Molding, PCBA Manufacturing, Automation, Cable Assembly, Cleanrooms, Polymer & Metal 3D Printing -> /", "Applications: Fluid & Gas Management, Surgical Energy, Optical Systems, Electromagnetic Navigation Systems & Sensors, Stimulation & Active Wearables, Consumables & Components -> /", "Customer: Conavi Medical (Tom Looby) -> /", "Customer: Fortune 500 Medical Device Manufacturer -> /", "Partnership with Vocxi Health for breath-based cancer detection device -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, CE Mark, RoHS -> db", "Scalable manufacturing from 10 units to 10 million -> /", "Vertically integrated in-house capabilities -> /", "Vital Link Portal for 24/7 access -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Forj Medical, a global medical device Contract Design and Manufacturing Organization (CDMO)", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "10 units", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='forj-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FormTight, Inc. was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Denver, Colorado. The custom plastic thermoforming company has operated for over three decades, specializing in both thin- and thick-gauge thermoforming for food, medical, industrial, and retail markets.

The company handles every stage of the packaging lifecycle in-house at its Denver facility, from consultation and design through prototyping, mold manufacturing, and full production. Capabilities include thin-gauge thermoforming for food and medical packaging, thick-gauge thermoforming for durable components, 5-axis CNC routing for complex geometries, and an in-house scrap grinding operation that recycles material back into the supply chain. Materials processed range from PET, PVC, ABS, HIPS, HDPE, PP, PETG, to polycarbonate.

FormTight serves manufacturers across food packaging, medical packaging, industrial thermoforming, and retail packaging. Long-term customers include Innovative Brick Systems and Dazzling Displays in Denver, Taylor Tools in Denver, Camerons Products in Colorado Springs, and Arm Automation in Austin, Texas. Testimonials highlight the firm''s ability to reengineer packaging for cost reduction, expedite aggressive schedules, and provide tooling expertise such as selecting male versus female tool designs.

FormTight emphasizes attention to detail, competitive pricing, on-time delivery, and high-quality finished products. The company states that keeping all processes under one roof gives it control over quality and lead times, while its sustainability focus closes the loop on waste through internal recycling. The team''s hands-on thermoforming experience and willingness to tackle challenging designs have retained customers for over three decades.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thin gauge thermoforming", "Thick gauge thermoforming", "Custom packaging design", "Rapid prototyping", "Mold manufacturing", "5-axis CNC routing", "In-house scrap grinding and recycling", "Tooling fabrication", "Consultation and design support"], "industries": ["Food packaging", "Medical packaging", "Industrial thermoforming", "Retail packaging"], "materials": ["PET (Polyethylene Terephthalate)", "PVC (Polyvinyl Chloride)", "ABS (Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene)", "HIPS (High Impact Polystyrene)", "HDPE (High Density Polyethylene)", "PP (Polypropylene)", "PETG (Polyethylene Terephthalate Glycol)", "PC (Polycarbonates)"], "equipment": ["5-axis CNC router", "In-house scrap grinding system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full in-house process from design through production", "In-house scrap grinding and recycling operation", "5-axis CNC routing for complex part geometries", "Rapid prototyping turnaround", "Tooling expertise including male/female tool selection"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1992 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Denver, CO -> /about-us", "Specializes in thin and thick gauge thermoforming -> /about-us", "Serves food, medical, industrial, retail industries -> /about-us", "In-house process: consultation, design, prototyping, mold manufacturing, production -> /about-us", "5-axis CNC routing capability -> /about-us", "In-house scrap grinding operation for sustainability -> /about-us", "Materials: PET, PVC, ABS, HIPS, HDPE, PP, PETG, PC -> /", "Customer examples: Innovative Brick Systems, Dazzling Displays, Taylor Tools, Camerons Products, Arm Automation -> /", "Testimonials from Vince Senia, Steve Weber, Dean Scott, Keith Papulski, Rachel McGee, Stephen Grupinski -> /about-us", "Rapid prototyping turnaround -> /services", "Tooling fabrication capability -> /services", "Male vs female tool selection expertise -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1992, FormTight is a custom plastic thermoforming company headquartered in Denver, CO.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='formtight-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, but it has established itself as a flexible packaging manufacturer serving a range of industrial and consumer markets.

The company produces a broad line of flexible packaging materials, including printed roll stock, pre-formed pouches, laminated films, heat-transfer labels, Inno-Lok® pre-zippered films, lidding films, cellophane and polypropylene bags, stand-up pouches, and both vertical form-fill-seal and flow-wrap packaging formats. Its film offerings cover high-moisture-barrier structures and oriented polypropylene (OPP and BOPP). In 2023 Formel added a 10-color W&H Miraflex printing press and installed a regenerative thermal oxidizer to reduce emissions, signaling investment in both print capability and environmental compliance.

Customers span medical device manufacturers, confectionery brands, private-label oil producers, and pail manufacturers. A senior buyer at a large medical corporation noted an "EXCELLENT" rating under ISO 13485 and FDA requirements, while a VP of procurement at a American confectioner and a purchasing manager at a private-label oil company have cited reliability and responsiveness.

Formel emphasizes on-time delivery and environmental responsibility. The regenerative thermal oxidizer and a published sustainability vision reflect a stated commitment to reducing its manufacturing footprint, and multiple customer testimonials highlight consistent delivery performance and cooperative handling of rush orders.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed roll stock", "Pre-formed pouches", "Laminated films", "Heat transfer labels", "Inno-Lok pre-zippered films", "Lidding films", "Cellophane & polypropylene bags", "Stand-up pouches & bags", "Vertical form fill seal packaging", "Flow wrap packaging", "High moisture barrier film", "Oriented polypropylene film (OPP & BOPP)"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Confectionery", "Private label oils", "Pail manufacturing", "Food packaging"], "materials": ["Cellophane", "Polypropylene", "Oriented polypropylene (OPP & BOPP)", "High moisture barrier films", "Laminated films"], "equipment": ["10-color W&H Miraflex press", "Regenerative thermal oxidizer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 13485 certification for medical-grade packaging", "10-color W&H Miraflex press for high-definition printing", "Regenerative thermal oxidizer for emissions control", "Inno-Lok\u00ae pre-zippered film capability", "Reputation for on-time delivery and rush-order flexibility"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Franklin Park, Illinois -> db", "ISO 13485 certification -> db", "Product list: printed roll stock, pre-formed pouches, laminated films, heat transfer labels, Inno-Lok pre-zippered films, lidding films, cellophane & polypropylene bags, stand-up pouches, VFFS, flow wrap, high moisture barrier film, OPP/BOPP -> /", "10-color W&H Miraflex press installed September 2023 -> /", "Regenerative thermal oxidizer installed July 2023 -> /", "Environmental sustainability vision January 2024 -> /", "Medical industry customer (large medical corporation) with ISO 13485/FDA r