UPDATE companies SET description='Forum Plastics LLC operates from Watertown, Connecticut. The company traces its roots to 1992 when GM Tool & Forum Molding Inc. was founded. In 2009, ownership was consolidated under Forum Plastics Inc., and in 2016 the business was acquired by Squadron Capital, a private equity group that reinvests proceeds into technology enhancements. The leadership team includes President Mark Polinsky and Vice President Andrew Butkus.

The company provides injection molding services with a focus on complex geometries, insert molding, over molding, and micro molding for parts as small as 0.005 cubic inches. It operates an ISO Class 7 cleanroom for assembly and packaging, and offers in-house mold design, fabrication, and repair through a full-service tool room equipped with CNC machining centers, EDM machines, and precision grinding. Additional capabilities include pad printing, laser marking, rapid prototyping, and advanced metrology such as industrial CT scanning, CMM, and VMM inspection. Monthly production volumes range from 100,000 to 200,000 parts, supported by a staff of 101 employees across a facility that added 10,000 square feet in 2015 and moved to a new location in December 2025.

Forum serves the medical device, life sciences, industrial, and military/defense markets. Its customer base spans early-stage startups to global original equipment manufacturers, with the company emphasizing support through concept planning, design for manufacturability, regulatory process navigation, and full-scale commercialization.

Forum differentiates itself as an engineering-based contract manufacturer that reinvests in new equipment—such as Arburg micro molders, Keyence measurement systems, and additive freeform 3D printing—to accelerate project timelines. The company highlights its ability to move from prototype to production in days rather than months, and its ITAR registration enables work on defense-related programs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2008','ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["ISO Class 7 cleanroom assembly", "Injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over molding", "Micro molding", "Rapid prototyping", "CNC machining", "EDM machining", "Pad printing", "Laser marking", "Mold design and fabrication", "Mold repair and modification", "CT scanning", "CMM inspection", "VMM inspection", "First article inspection", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "PPAP", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Project management", "Serialization", "Press-fit assembly", "Kitting", "Sterile packaging coordination"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Life sciences", "Industrial", "Military/Defense"], "materials": ["Medical-grade polymers", "Engineering-grade resins"], "equipment": ["BOY Mini Molders", "Arburg Shuttle Press", "Arburg Micro Molders", "Arburg 220 & 270 Ton Molding Cells", "Keyence IM", "Keyence IL", "CT Scanner", "3D Systems Printer", "Filament 3D Printer", "Additive Freeform 3D Printer", "MoldFlow simulation software", "IQMS ERP system", "CNC machining centers", "EDM machines", "Precision grinding and polishing centers"], "volume": "100,000-200,000 parts per month", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO Class 7 cleanroom molding and assembly", "Micro molding for parts as small as 0.005 in\u00b3", "In-house mold design, fabrication, and repair", "Industrial CT scanning for non-destructive first article inspection"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 as GM Tool & Forum Molding Inc. -> /about-us", "Acquired by Squadron Capital in 2016 -> /about-us", "101 employees overseen by Director of Operations -> /about-us", "ISO Class 7 cleanroom assembly -> /capabilities", "Injection molding, insert/over molding, micro molding -> /capabilities", "Monthly production 100,000-200,000 parts -> /", "Industries: Medical, Industrial, Military/Defense -> /", "Certifications: ISO 13485:2016, ISO 9001:2008, ISO 14001:2015, ITAR -> /quality, /about-us", "Equipment: Arburg, BOY, Keyence, CT Scanner, 3D printers -> /about-us", "Facility: 10,000 sq ft addition 2015, new facility Dec 2025 -> /about-us", "Leadership: Mark Polinsky, Andrew Butkus, etc. -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a contract manufacturer, Forum is available to help get your project running from start to finish.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "101", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='forum-plastics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Four Engines Apparel operates from a dedicated shop at 201B West Boylston Street in West Boylston, Massachusetts. The company was established in 2020 by Dave Keddy, who began the venture as a home-based business in his basement before growing a customer base that supported a move into a standalone facility. Keddy brought over 17 years of prior experience in logo merchandising and apparel decoration to the operation.

The shop provides embroidery, screen printing, custom patches, and heat transfers on a range of apparel and fabric types. Work is performed in-house, allowing direct control over each decoration process. The owner emphasizes personal communication and attention to detail across every order, from single items to larger runs, without publishing specific facility dimensions or headcount figures.

Customers include local small businesses, musical acts, sports teams such as youth soccer programs, and specialty organizations like Expedition Reptile, which uses embroidered show shirts for weekly performances. The business explicitly positions itself to serve low-quantity orders that larger contract decorators often decline, targeting community groups, startups, and independent brands needing branded gear in smaller volumes.

Keddy cites a dual motivation: a passion for the rhythm of production processes — likened to his background as a musician — and a long-term goal to create or partner with a charity that funds community music programs. The name "Four Engines" originates from a drumming term that has resonated with him since a lesson years ago.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Embroidery", "Screen printing", "Custom patches", "Heat transfers"], "industries": ["Music and entertainment", "Youth and amateur sports", "Small business branding", "Community organizations", "Reptile shows and exhibitions"], "materials": ["Cotton apparel", "Polyester apparel", "Blended fabrics", "Various garment types (hats, jackets, shirts)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Accepts low-quantity orders that larger facilities decline", "Direct owner communication and personal customer service", "Over 17 years of owner experience in logo merchandising", "Grown from home-based basement operation to dedicated shop"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2020 -> / and /about", "Location West Boylston, MA -> / and /about", "Owner Dave Keddy -> / (reviews)", "Started home-based, moved to shop -> / and /about", "Services: embroidery, screen printing, patches, transfers -> / and /about", "17 years owner experience in logo merchandising -> /about", "Serves low-quantity orders -> /about", "Customers: bands, brands, soccer teams, Expedition Reptile -> / (reviews)", "Name from drumming term, music charity goal -> /about", "Address 201B W Boylston St -> / and /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Established in 2020, Four Engines Apparel began as a home-based company dedicated to quality decorations and personal customer service.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='four-engines-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Four Fields Furniture operates from West St. Paul, Minnesota, in the Twin Cities metro area. Bischoff, a craftsman, started building pieces by hand for local clients, emphasizing solid hardwoods and steel accents.

The shop produces made-to-order hardwood furniture, specializing in dining tables (including live-edge slab designs), coffee tables, side tables, desks, entryway benches, sideboards, bookshelves, and wood-and-steel combinations. It also builds custom religious items such as kneelers, altars, and credence tables, and offers professional table refinishing.

Four Fields serves residential customers throughout the Twin Cities, including Minneapolis, St. Paul, and surrounding suburbs. Its clientele consists primarily of homeowners seeking custom pieces for their homes, with the company noting trust from "Twin Cities families" and over 100 five-star Google reviews. Delivery and setup are provided across the metro area.

