UPDATE companies SET description='GAI Energy, based in Flora, Indiana, was founded in 2008 when two electrical engineers, Chris Rohaly and Neal Rhodes, combined their 60 years of electrical design and troubleshooting experience to launch a renewable energy venture in Kokomo. The company now operates from Flora, serving north central Indiana.

As an EPC solar contractor, GAI Energy delivers turnkey commercial and industrial solar plus battery storage systems. The firm handles every stage in-house — from engineering and permitting to installation and ongoing maintenance — covering projects from kilowatt-scale arrays to multi-megawatt installations.

The company works with farmers, business owners, and industrial clients in communities such as Lafayette, Plymouth, Valparaiso, and Carmel. Its agricultural and commercial customers rely on GAI for microgrid solutions that provide energy security and reduce utility costs.

