UPDATE companies SET description='GOEX Apparel operates from Kansas City, Missouri, where it manages printing, warehousing, and distribution for a supply chain that spans the Western Hemisphere. The company is structured as a certified B-Corp and verified member of the Fair Trade Federation, Social Enterprise Alliance, and Fair Labor Association, though its founding year and original founders are not publicly disclosed.

The company produces custom-printed apparel and wholesale blank basics, including eco-triblend tees. Fabrics are knitted in South Carolina from U.S.-sourced materials, then cut and sewn at GOEX''s owned factory in Haiti. Finished garments are printed and shipped from the Kansas City facility, creating a 2,700-mile supply chain—far shorter than the industry average of six global circumnavigations.

GOEX serves organizations needing branded merchandise, retail-ready wholesale basics, and tour merchandise for musicians. Its customer base includes the Minnesota Historical Society, Black Hills Basecamp, Biomes Marine Biology Center, and Koraa, all cited as verified buyers.

The business was built to create fair-wage jobs in Haiti, paying 65 percent above the local apparel-sector minimum so that each employee can support an average of six family members. It also prioritizes OEKO-TEX ECO PASSPORT certified fabrics and Fair Trade certified labels, positioning every order as a driver of family stability and reduced environmental impact.', certifications=ARRAY['Fair Trade Federation Verified','B-Corp Certified','Social Enterprise Alliance Verified','Fair Labor Association','Social Enterprise World Forum','OEKO-TEX ECO PASSPORT','FAIR TRADE','OEKO-TEX']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom printed apparel", "Wholesale blank apparel", "Cut and sew manufacturing", "Screen printing", "Sustainable fabric sourcing", "Fair trade manufacturing", "Fabric knitting", "Warehousing and distribution"], "industries": ["Wholesale apparel", "Custom printed apparel", "Music merchandise", "Branded organizational apparel", "Retail basics"], "materials": ["U.S.-grown cotton", "Eco-Triblend fabric", "OEKO-TEX certified fabrics", "Fair Trade certified labels and tags"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pays 65% above Haiti''s apparel sector minimum wage", "2,700-mile supply chain from U.S. fabric to Haitian cut-and-sew to Kansas City printing", "B-Corp certified and Fair Trade Federation verified", "OEKO-TEX ECO PASSPORT certified fabrics", "U.S.-grown fabrics cut and sewn in the Western Hemisphere"], "facts_used": ["HQ city/state -> db", "Factory in Haiti, fabrics from South Carolina, printing in Kansas City -> homepage", "Certifications (Fair Trade Federation, B-Corp, Social Enterprise Alliance, Fair Labor Association, Social Enterprise World Forum) -> about page", "Certifications (FAIR TRADE, OEKO-TEX) -> db", "Fair wage: 65% above Haiti minimum -> about page", "2700 mile supply chain -> homepage", "Customers (Minnesota Historical Society, Black Hills Basecamp, Biomes Marine Biology Center, Koraa) -> about 