UPDATE companies SET description='General Spring of Kansas City, Inc. operates from New Century, Kansas, and traces its roots to 1965 when Paul Flood founded the business as a full-service leaf spring repair shop in the Kansas City area.

Today the firm stocks and sells a broad line of suspension components—front and rear leaf springs, coil springs, U-bolts, shackles, shocks, and add-a-leaf kits—for everything from late-model pickups to classic hot rods. It maintains an 18,000-square-foot warehouse in the Kansas City metro and ships from multiple distribution points nationwide. In addition to distributing products from suppliers such as Dayton Parts (Stanley Spring), Universal Group, and APM Auto, General Spring runs an in-house shop that can modify or custom-fabricate leaf springs, including swapping stock clips for riveted metal clips to increase strength.

Catalog coverage includes Ford, Chevrolet, Dodge, Jeep, Toyota, and Nissan applications, with specific listings for trucks, SUVs, and older performance vehicles.

General Spring differentiates itself by working only with manufacturers that belong to the Spring Research Institute, visually inspecting every part before shipment, and backing all replacement leaf springs with a one-year warranty. The company emphasizes that its products meet or exceed OEM specifications and that most stock orders ship within 24 hours, a speed it contrasts with big-box retailers and overseas drop-shippers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Leaf spring manufacturing and modification", "Custom leaf spring fabrication", "Leaf spring inspection and quality control", "Warehousing and distribution", "Expedited shipping (24-hour)", "Suspension repair services", "Add-a-leaf kit installation", "U-bolt and shackle replacement"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Truck and SUV suspension", "Classic car and hot rod restoration", "Suspension repair professionals", "DIY automotive enthusiasts"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "24 hours for stock items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exclusive one-year warranty on all replacement leaf springs", "Products meet or exceed OEM specifications", "In-house manufacturing and modification capabilities for custom leaf springs", "Same-day shipping on stocked items (24 hours)", "Work exclusively with Spring Research Institute (SRI) member manufacturers", "Visual inspection of all parts before shipping"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 by Paul Flood -> /about-us", "Headquarters in New Century, Kansas -> db", "18,000-square-foot facility since 2014 -> /about-us", "In-house manufacturing and modification capabilities -> /", "Work with SRI member manufacturers -> /", "One-year warranty on replacement leaf springs -> /", "24-hour shipping on most items -> /", "Serve DIY enthusiasts and suspension repair professionals -> /", "Products for Ford, Chevrolet, Dodge, imports, SUVs, hot rods -> /", "Brands: Chevrolet, Ford, Jeep, Toyota, Nissan -> /about-us", "Suppliers: Dayton Parts, Universal Group, APM Auto -> /about-us", "Family ownership history: Paul Flood, Jim Flood, Jim Jr., Joe Wallace -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We warehouse leaf springs at our Kansas City location along with shipping from manufacturers and suppliers such as Dayton Parts (Stanley Spring), Universal Group, APM Auto and others", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='general-spring-of-kansas-city-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='General Woodworking Inc. is a family-owned architectural millwork manufacturer based in Lowell, Massachusetts. Founded in 1978, the company has served general contractors and end users across New England for over four decades. Current ownership is held by John Thompson, Sara Axon, and Dan Thompson, who oversee a management team that includes project engineers, sales, and inside sales staff.

The firm operates a 46,300-square-foot, solar-powered manufacturing facility where it produces custom architectural millwork and decorative laid-up panels for industry partners. Capabilities span project management from design through installation, with drafting performed to AWI Quality Certification Program (QCP) standards. The shop holds AWI QCP certification, FSC® Chain-of-Custody certification (FSC® C106456) for responsibly sourced lumber and veneer, and is equipped to meet LEED v4 requirements. A notable portion of the workforce has remained with the company for 20 to 30 years, preserving institutional knowledge.

The company also supplies laid-up panels to other woodworking industry partners.

General Woodworking emphasizes fair pricing, exceptional quality, and reasonable lead times as core differentiators. Its investment in solar power and FSC certification reflects a commitment to reducing environmental impact, while the long-tenured staff ensures consistency and deep expertise on complex millwork projects.', certifications=ARRAY['AWI QCP','FSC® COC (FSC® C106456)','LEED v4']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural millwork (custom)", "Decorative laid-up panels", "Project management (design through installation)", "Drafting to AWI QCP standards", "LEED v4 compliance support"], "industries": ["Architectural millwork", "Commercial construction", "General contractors", "End users (residential and commercial)", "Woodworking industry partners"], "materials": ["Lumber", "Veneer"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with a focus on fair pricing, exceptional quality, and reasonable lead times", "46,300 sq. ft. solar-powered manufacturing facility in Lowell, MA", "AWI QCP certified for architectural millwork standards", "FSC\u00ae COC certified (FSC\u00ae C106456) for responsibly harvested lumber and veneer", "Workforce retention with many employees at 20+ years and some at 30+ years"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1978 -> db", "Headquarters Lowell, Massachusetts -> db", "Family-owned business -> /about", "46,300 sq. ft. solar-powered manufacturing facility -> /about", "Capabilities: decorative laid-up panels, architectural millwork projects start to finish -> /about", "AWI QCP certified -> /about", "FSC\u00ae COC certified (FSC\u00ae C106456) -> /about", "LEED v4 requirements -> /about", "Ownership: John Thompson, Sara Axon, Dan Thompson -> /about", "Employees with 20-30 year tenure -> /about", "Serves general contractors and end users throughout New England -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We operate out of our own 46,300 sq. ft. solar powered manufacturing facility in historic Lowell, Massachusetts.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/general-woodworking-inc/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='general-woodworking-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Gentry Plastics, Inc. operates a 40,000-square-foot plastics manufacturing facility in Gastonia, North Carolina.

Its core capabilities include injection molding, overmolding, sonic welding, plastic machining, assembly, and pack-out services. A dedicated customer service department manages projects from initial design through production, and a company-owned delivery truck supports local clients. The plant recently underwent an expansion to increase capacity.

The manufacturer serves a diverse industrial base spanning aerospace, agricultural equipment, appliances, automotive, electronics, marine, military, packaging, plumbing, and metal-replacement applications. Customers also include custom projects outside these categories.

