UPDATE companies SET description='Gentuity, LLC is based in Sudbury, Massachusetts. The company was founded by alumni of the original LightLab team, the group that pioneered the first-generation optical coherence tomography (OCT) systems deployed in catheterization laboratories worldwide. Drawing on decades of experience in intravascular imaging, the founders set out to overcome the limitations of traditional OCT technology.

The system is designed for plug-and-play integration into existing cath lab workflows without requiring sterile bags.

Gentuity serves interventional cardiologists and hospital catheterization labs focused on complex percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) procedures. Clinical case studies feature physicians from Tampa General Hospital and The Christ Hospital. In the United States, the company''s advanced intravascular imaging solutions are distributed through a partnership with GE HealthCare.

The venture was launched to address the shortcomings of conventional OCT systems, aiming to provide complete vessel visualization and real-time insights that enable confident treatment planning. By combining expertise in optics, software, and interventional cardiology, Gentuity seeks to simplify complex procedures and advance cardiovascular innovation in line with international guidelines.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HF-OCT imaging system manufacturing", "Micro-imaging catheter manufacturing (1.8F Vis-Rx PRIME)", "Intravascular imaging technology development", "Clinical case study support", "Physician education and training resources"], "industries": ["Cardiovascular medical devices", "Interventional cardiology", "Medical imaging", "Percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["High-frequency OCT (HF-OCT) imaging technology", "Ultra-low-profile 1.8F Vis-Rx PRIME micro-imaging catheter", "Single-pullback, full-length coronary imaging in one second", "Plug-and-play cath lab integration without sterile bags", "U.S. distribution partnership with GE HealthCare"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Sudbury, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded by original LightLab team members -> /about-us", "Develops HF-OCT Imaging System and 1.8F Vis-Rx PRIME Micro-Imaging Catheter -> /", "Single-pullback full-length imaging in one second -> /", "Plug-and-play integration without sterile bags -> /", "Partnership with GE HealthCare for U.S. distribution -> /", "Clinical case studies from Tampa General Hospital and The Christ Hospital -> /", "Mission to address limitations of traditional OCT systems -> /about-us", "Trademarks: HF-OCT, One Second Imaging, Vis-Rx -> /", "Copyright 2026 Gentuity, LLC -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Gentuity is pioneering the next generation of intravascular imaging. Through high-frequency O