UPDATE companies SET description='George C. Moore operates from Westerly, Rhode Island, where the company was founded in 1909 as the George C. Moore Company. The business remains a privately held, family-owned enterprise and serves as the parent of two wholly owned divisions: George C. Moore Company, which produces stretch and rigid narrow fabrics in woven and knit constructions, and Darlington Fabrics, which manufactures stretch and rigid wide warp knit fabrics.

The company manufactures narrow elastic fabrics and rigid webbings for a range of end uses. Its U.S. headquarters in Westerly houses sales, engineering, design, research and development, and technical support, while a vertical weaving and knitting facility established in 2006 in American Park Free Zone, El Salvador, handles production from ¼-inch to 12-inch widths. That site also provides in-house dyeing and finishing, rotary printing, cutting and sewing, performance finishes, and customized packaging.

Customers span swim, dance, and yoga apparel; underwear waistbands and trims; ballistic protection for military and law enforcement; flame-resistant work uniforms; safety and industrial webbing; team sports gear such as goggles and pads; performance compression and activewear; and orthopedic and medical products including latex-free, hook-receptive, and plush-surface elastics.

The founding premise of “providing continual innovation and support to our valued customers” has guided the company for over 110 years. It emphasizes competitive pricing, consistent quality, and on-time delivery, backed by two R&D divisions and sustainability programs that have cut heating and cooling energy by 35%, lighting energy by 40%, water usage by 44%, and achieved recycling rates of 33% for wooden pallets, 15% for corrugated boxes, and 100% for plastic process bags.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Narrow elastic fabric manufacturing (woven and knit)", "Rigid narrow fabric manufacturing (woven and knit)", "Wide warp knit fabric manufacturing (Darlington Fabrics)", "Rigid webbing manufacturing", "Dyeing and finishing", "Rotary printing", "Cutting and sewing", "Performance finishes (flame resistant, technical)", "Customized packaging", "Research and development", "Design and engineering support", "Technical consultation", "Manufacturing consultation", "Quality assurance"], "industries": ["Swimwear", "Dancewear", "Yoga apparel", "Underwear", "Ballistic protection", "Military uniforms", "Law enforcement", "Work apparel", "Uniforms", "Safety equipment", "Industrial webbing", "Team sports", "Performance compression", "Active apparel", "Orthopedic", "Medical", "Stretch loop"], "materials": ["Sustainable yarns (natural and recycled)", "Latex-free elastic", "Hook-receptive fabrics", "Plush-surface fabrics", "Flame-resistant finishes"], "equipment": ["Vertical weaving machines", "Knitting machines", "Dyeing and finishing equipment", "Rotary printing equipment", "Cutting and sewing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Preferred market leader for over 110 years", "Vertical weaving and knitting operation in El Salvador (\u00bc\"\u201312\" width)", "In-house dyeing, finishing, rotary printing, cutting, sewing, and packaging", "Two dedicated R&D divisions for new elastic and webbing development", "Documented energy, water, and waste reductions (35\u201344% cuts, high recycling rates)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1909 -> /about-us", "Headquartered Westerly, Rhode Island -> /about-us", "Privately held family-owned business -> /about-us", "Two divisions: George C. Moore Company and Darlington Fabrics -> /about-us", "El Salvador facility since 2006, American Park Free Zone -> /about-us", "Vertical weaving/knitting, 1/4\" to 12\" width -> /about-us", "In-house dyeing & finishing, rotary printing, cutting & sewing, performance finishes, packaging -> /about-us", "Industries: swim/dance/yoga, underwear, ballistic protection, work apparel, safety/industrial, team sports, performance compression/active, orthopedic/medical/stretch loop -> /", "Sustainability metrics: 35% heating/cooling, 40% lighting, 33% equipment energy reduction; 44% water reduction; recycling rates -> /about-us", "R&D divisions mentioned -> /", "Latex-free, hook receptive, plush surfaces -> /", "Flame resistant finishes -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufacturer of stretch and rigid narrow fabric (woven and knit) ... manufacturer of stretch and rigid wide warp knit fabric", "founded_year": "1909", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='george-c-moore' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded more than 30 years ago, George''s Apparel has operated continuously from its Manchester, New Hampshire location, serving clients throughout New England. The retailer occupies a storefront at the corner of Elm Street and Central Avenue, though specific ownership structure and founder names are not disclosed.

The store carries an extensive selection of suits, jackets, dress shirts, and footwear sourced from manufacturers such as Ralph Lauren, Calvin Klein, S. Cohen, Mantoni, Michael Kors, and Hart Schaffner Marx, along with footwear lines from Florsheim, Clarks, Johnston & Murphy, and Bostonian. A fully staffed tailor shop handles alterations for items purchased on-site as well as garments brought in from other retailers, supported by a sales team whose combined experience spans over 200 years.

The clientele ranges from professionals needing workwear to wedding parties and students attending proms, with the company noting a focus on special-occasion attire across the New England area.

