UPDATE companies SET description='Getinge operates from Merrimack, New Hampshire, as the U.S. headquarters of a global medical technology group with roots tracing to 1838 when Maquet was founded in Germany. The Getinge Group took shape through a series of acquisitions: Maquet in 2000 brought operating-room tables and surgical workflows, followed by Jostra (heart-lung machines) and Siemens LSS (ventilators) in 2003, expanding the portfolio into acute care therapies.

The company designs and manufactures equipment for intensive care, cardiovascular procedures, operating rooms, sterile processing, pharmaceutical production, and research laboratories.

Getinge states its purpose as a "passion for life," aiming to stand behind every life saved and breakthrough made. The heritage of firsts — such as the world''s first motorized operating table and the table used in the first heart transplant — is presented as the foundation for its focus on patient-centric, personalized ventilation and sterile processing solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ventilator manufacturing", "Operating table manufacturing", "Heart-lung machine manufacturing", "Sterile processing equipment", "Pharmaceutical production equipment", "Bioreactor systems", "Control systems", "Software development", "Analytics", "Perfusion systems", "Biocontainment systems", "Fluorescence imaging compatible surgical lights"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Medical Devices", "Pharmaceutical Production", "Research Laboratories", "Intensive Care", "Cardiovascular Procedures", "Operating Room", "Sterile Processing", "Vaccine Production", "Bioprocessing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Servo Ventilator", "Servo-air Lite", "Maquet Volista", "DPTE\u00ae-EXO Alpha Port", "Production Scale Bioreactors", "Production Scale Control Systems", "Production Scale Perfusion Systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Heritage of medical firsts including first motorized OR table and first heart transplant table", "Integrated acute care portfolio spanning ventilation, cardiopulmonary, and OR", "Personalized ventilation technology via Servo platform", "Sterile processing and biocontainment for pharmaceutical production", "Global support network with multi-language service"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1838 (Maquet) -> db description", "Acquisition of Maquet in 2000 -> db description", "Acquisition of Jostra and Siemens LSS in 2003 -> db description", "HQ Merrimack, NH -> db hq_city/hq_state_label", "Products: ventilators, operating tables, heart-lung machines, sterile processing, pharmaceutical production, bioreactors, c