UPDATE companies SET description='Gil Sewing Corp. operates from Morton Grove, Illinois, a Chicago suburb. Today it is a family‑run, women‑ and minority‑owned enterprise that has grown to employ several hundred sewing operators.

The firm provides a turnkey apparel service covering design, development, cut‑and‑sew manufacturing, in‑house embroidery, and global sourcing from nine partner countries. Its 56,000‑square‑foot domestic facility is fully automated, featuring Gerber GtXL cutters capable of 30‑ply cuts and computerized sewing machines with servo motors. Production runs from small batches to large‑scale orders, with all domestic work — cutting, sewing, finishing, and shipping — handled under one roof.

Clients span uniform suppliers, fashion brands, retail labels, and government agencies such as the Naval Center for Research and Testing. The product range includes tailored suits, shirts, bottoms, outerwear, knits, flame‑resistant garments, dresses, dress uniforms, activewear, dog apparel, and upholstery. Both domestic and overseas orders are developed in Chicago before being sent to partner factories in Mexico, China, El Salvador, Thailand, Vietnam, Kenya, Ethiopia, and Egypt.

The company emphasizes a “perfection” philosophy built on rigorous quality control: DOD‑certified final audit testing, a consistent sub‑2.5 AQL, in‑process inspections at every operation, and dedicated auditors who travel to overseas plants multiple times per order. Its central location enables three‑day shipping anywhere in the United States.', certifications=ARRAY['DOD certified for final audit testing']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design", "Development", "Cut-and-sew manufacturing", "Embroidery (custom and contract)", "Sourcing (global, 9 countries)", "Automated cutting (Gerber GtXL)", "Computerized sewing (servo motor)", "Finishing", "Quality auditing (in-process and final)", "Pattern making", "Sample production", "Tech pack development", "Overseas production management", "Fabric inspection", "Grading and marking"], "industries": ["Uniforms", "Fashion apparel", "Retail apparel", "Military/Defense (DOD)", "Tailored clothing", "Workwear", "Activewear", "Outerwear", "Flame-resistant (FR) apparel", "Pet apparel", "Upholstery"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Gerber GtXL cutters (30-ply)", "Computerized sewing machines with servo motors"], "volume": "Small to large scale production", "lead_time": "Quick turn times; 3-day shipping to anywhere in US", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["DOD\u2011certified final audit testing with sub\u20112.5 AQL across all customers", "In\u2011process quality auditing at every production operation", "56,000 sq ft fully automated domestic facility with Gerber GtXL 30\u2011ply cutters", "Domestic pattern and sample development before any overseas production", "Three\u2011day shipping to any U.S. destination from Chicago\u2011area plant"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Morton Grove, Illinois -> db", "Founder Michael Kaham started company in 1992 -> /", "Formally established May 20, 1993 -> /about-us", "Women Minority Owned Business -> /about-us", "Family company run with family values -> /", "56,000 sq ft fully automated facility -> /about-us", "Gerber GtXL cutters up to 30 ply -> /about-us", "Computerized sewing machines with servo motors -> /about-us", "Domestic and offshore operations in 9 countries -> /about-us", "DOD certified for final audit testing -> /about-us", "Less than 2.5 AQL -> /about-us", "In-process auditing at every operation -> /about-us", "Three-day shipping anywhere in US -> /about-us", "Products: tailored apparel, dresses, overcoats, trousers, vests, blouses, shirts, slacks, coats, knits, FR apparel -> /about-us", "Services: Design, Development, Manufacturing, Embroidery, Sourcing -> /services", "Small to large scale production -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a garment manufacture of male and female uniforms, tailored and work clothing and retail apparel.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Minority-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gil-sewing-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Glaser Steel, a family-owned steel supplier and fabricator, has operated in Colorado Springs, Colorado since 1945. It began as H & G Welding, founded by Eugene Glaser and his brother-in-law Frank Holley in a former horse stable on Cucharras Street. Eugene later became sole owner, renaming it Glaser Welding Works, and his son Burton ''Buddy'' Glaser joined the shop after high school. The business relocated to its present address at 619 South 31st Street in 1969 after the city acquired the downtown property.

The company stocks mild steel and aluminum in full lengths and sells by the inch, also offering a drop pile of remnants. Its shop provides custom saw cutting, shearing, drilling, punching, welding and fabrication, and CNC plasma cutting of sheets and plates. A 2005 expansion added capacity for larger plate inventory and a plasma cutting table. Glaser Steel also delivers materials and finished fabrications to local job sites.

Glaser Steel serves customers throughout the Front Range region, including retail buyers, contractors, and fabrication shops that need custom metalwork or raw stock. The business has remained under family control through multiple generations; it is currently operated by Jacque and Tony Jensen, the daughter and son-in-law of Buddy Glaser.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail sales of mild steel and aluminum", "Custom saw cutting", "Shearing", "Drilling", "Punching", "Welding and fabrication", "CNC plasma cutting", "Delivery"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Mild steel", "Aluminum", "Steel sheets", "Steel plates"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma cutting table"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Retail sales by the inch", "Drop pile of remnants available", "CNC plasma cutting of custom shapes", "Delivery of materials and fabricated items", "Family-owned and operated since 1945"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1945 -> /about-us", "Founders Eugene Glaser and Frank Holley -> /about-us", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "Location Colorado Springs, CO -> db", "Current address 619 S. 31st Street -> /about-us", "Services: retail sales, custom saw cutting, shearing, drilling, punching, welding & fabrication, CNC plasma cutting, delivery -> /services", "Materials: mild steel and aluminum -> /services", "Plasma table added 2005 -> /about-us", "Operated by Jacque and Tony Jensen -> /about-us", "Serves Front Range region -> /about-us", "Sell by the inch -> /services", "Drop pile available -> /services", "Delivery offered -> /services", "CNC plasma cutting table -> /about-us, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Welding & Fabrication ... we are able to build your project ... CNC Plasma Cutting ... we can cut out almost any shape out of steel sheets or plates.", "founded_year": "1945", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='glaser-steel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Glenn A. Hissim Woodworking operates a family-owned custom woodworking manufacturing facility in Kintnersville, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1991 by Glenn Hissim, who brought over 35 years of industry experience, the company began as a consultation, design, and build operation for custom architectural pieces.

The shop produces architectural millwork, custom kitchen cabinets, bathroom vanities, libraries, built-in furniture, bookcases, fireplace surrounds and mantles, wainscoting, and entrance ways. A climate-controlled plant with radiant heated floors maintains consistent material temperatures, enabling exact tolerances during joinery. An in-house design team develops projects to client specifications before any production begins.

The company serves residential and commercial clients, including homeowners, businesses, architects, and designers. Projects range from single vanities to complete library installations, with each engagement starting with a face-to-face consultation attended by Glenn Hissim himself to review materials and installation approaches.

